<title>NETHERLANDS: Swedish PM sees no weakening or delay of EMU.</title>
<headline>Swedish PM sees no weakening or delay of EMU.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-06-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish Prime Minister Goran Persson said on Sunday he saw no risk that the Franco-German rift over a stability pact would weaken or delay economic and monetary union (EMU).</p>
<p>&quot;No, I don't see any risk at all in that,&quot; Persson told reporters in response to a direct question.</p>
</text>
